[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":90},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":88,"_13":88,"_42":89},"id","basico","nome","Beginner method","nomeLongo","Layers, with the Sune and the T-perm","termo",{"_42":85,"_86":87},"niveis",[47],"introducao","<p>The way to solve the 2x2 for the first time: the bottom layer, then the top one, with just two algorithms, the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sune\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two short OLL algorithms that orient 3 corners: R U R' U R U2 R' (Sune) and R U2 R' U' R U' R' (Anti-Sune).\">Sune</a> and the headlights one. They&#39;re the same as in the 3x3 <a href=\"/en/glossary#basico\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Most people's first method: it solves the cube layer by layer, in 8 steps, with few algorithms. It's slow, but it teaches how the pieces…\">beginner method</a>: if you know the 3x3, you know the 2x2.</p>\n","etapas",[27,28,29],"historias",[],{"_11":77,"_13":78,"_32":79,"_34":80,"_36":81,"_38":-7,"_40":82},{"_11":57,"_13":58,"_32":59,"_34":60,"_36":61,"_38":62,"_40":63},{"_11":30,"_13":31,"_32":33,"_34":35,"_36":37,"_38":39,"_40":41},"cantos","Corners in place","html","<p>The top corners in the right place, by looking for headlights. The end: the cube solved.</p>\n","grupos",[44],"pagina",{"_13":31,"_42":43},"treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=basico/cantos/casos","imagem","/imagens/diagramas/02b6a512b5070e6c.svg","endereco","/2x2/basico/cantos",{"_11":45,"_13":31,"_46":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_42":54},"2x2 Passo 3","nivel","iniciante","casos",2,"conjunto",false,"ids",[55,56],"/2x2/basico/cantos/casos","2X2-B3-Dois-cantos-certos","2X2-B3-Nenhum-par-certo","face-amarela","Yellow face","<p>The top corners with yellow facing up, with the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sune\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two short OLL algorithms that orient 3 corners: R U R' U R U2 R' (Sune) and R U2 R' U' R U' R' (Anti-Sune).\">Sune</a>.</p>\n",[65],{"_13":58,"_42":64},"/2x2/treino?grupo=basico/face-amarela/casos","/imagens/diagramas/085c13cc78086489.svg","/2x2/basico/face-amarela",{"_11":66,"_13":58,"_46":47,"_48":67,"_50":51,"_52":68,"_42":69},"2x2 Passo 2",7,[70,71,72,73,74,75,76],"/2x2/basico/face-amarela/casos","2X2-B2-Peixe-Sune","2X2-B2-Peixe-Anti-Sune","2X2-B2-Cruz-H","2X2-B2-Pi","2X2-B2-Farois","2X2-B2-T","2X2-B2-Gravata","primeira-camada","1st layer","<p>The white corners on the bottom, with the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sexy-move\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The trigger R U R' U', the most common of all.\">sexy move</a> (<code>R U R&#39; U&#39;</code>), and the bottom sides matching.</p>\n",[],{"_13":83,"_42":84},"/imagens/diagramas/c45a8b8ff00c6670.svg","1st face","/2x2/primeira-face","/en/glossary#basico","dica","Most people's first method: it solves the cube layer by layer, in 8 steps, with few algorithms. It's slow, but it teaches how the pieces…","2x2","/2x2/",{"_91":92,"_93":94},"cubos",[97,98,99,100,101,102,103],"idiomas",[95,96],"pt","en",{"_11":112,"_13":112},{"_11":88,"_13":88},{"_11":111,"_13":111},{"_11":110,"_13":110},{"_11":108,"_13":109},{"_11":106,"_13":107},{"_11":104,"_13":105},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
